NNAAMMEE
     ssttaattss — information about various and sundry statistics utilities

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The FreeBSD userland in part contains a series of utilities which can be
     used to ascertain system state at runtime and optionally from core files.

CCOOMMMMAANNDDSS
     The following commands (sorted alphabetically) are currently included in
     the base system, with more appearing periodically.

     bbttssoocckkssttaatt    Show Bluetooth socket information

     ccttllssttaatt       CAM Target Layer statistics utility

     ddwwaattcchh        Watch processes as they trigger a particular DTrace probe

     ffssttaatt         Identify active files

     ggssttaatt         Print statistics about GEOM disks

     iibbssttaatt        Display information from the InfiniBand driver

     iiffmmccssttaatt      Dump multicast group management statistics per interface

     iioossttaatt        Report kernel subsystem I/O statistics

     iippffssttaatt       Display IPF packet filter statistics and filter list

     kkllddssttaatt       Display status of dynamic kernel linker

     lloocckkssttaatt      Report kernel lock and profiling statistics

     mmaaiillssttaattss     Display mail statistics

     nneettssttaatt       Show network status and statistics

     nnffssssttaatt       Display NFS statistics

     pplloocckkssttaatt     Trace pthread lock statistics using DTrace

     ppmmccssttaatt       Performance measurement with performance monitoring hard‐
                   ware

     pprrooccssttaatt      Get detailed process information

     ppssttaatt         Display system data structures

     ssoocckkssttaatt      List open sockets

     ssttaatt          Display file status

     ssyyssttaatt        Display system statistics

     vvmmssttaatt        Report virtual memory statistics

     zzppooooll iioossttaatt  Report ZFS I/O statistics

